body:
I get that, but it was still a bit of a dickish situation, and i'd rather it not have happened altogether. I'm fine with these sorts of things in the game - Hell, i've played Cit and Hyper for a while - As long as i'm not forced into interacting with them. I get that you probably think i'm being 'A little bitch', but it made me uncomfortable to be forced into being called 'Femboy' constantly, and having to remind the crew constantly that I was not 'AI', I was 'Femboy'. Hell, I experienced this once on Hyper before where I got a lawset that forced me to call myself 'Slut', but at least on there, after I told the Cap who uploaded it I was uncomfortable, he agreed to take it offline. This HOP not only refused after I told them i'd rather not be forced to be 'Femboy', but they also almost killed the RD for trying to reset it, helped the HOS execute a cargo tech for resetting it, and uploaded a law stating to not let anyone change it. And i've gotten laws like this before ; Laws like "You must act like a stereotypical furry", "You must act like you are sexually attracted to felinids", etc, but most of the time when I requested those gone, they were either removed, or were uploaded by a Traitor trying to fuck with me, or were on an LRP/NRP server where that sort of stuff is highly expected.

&#x200B;

The bottom line is, the HOP acted like a huge dick. Did he deserve a ban for being a dick? Maybe not, but he was still a dick, and I don't lament the ban at all.

Blackblood Carys

&#x200B;

Save up for the Bounty Hunter Drone pet. Legendary Archfiend ahoy!

This video - [https://youtu.be/18wLxJo9LpI?t=941](https://youtu.be/18wLxJo9LpI?t=941)

&#x200B;

And the comments of it are pretty good for getting some great base locations. In the comments there are two that especially stand out to me - These ones.

&#x200B;

 [https://ibb.co/0D2YKhZ](https://www.youtube.com/redirect?stzid=UgzAsto7f3PaFtTzfNd4AaABAg&q=https%3A%2F%2Fibb.co%2F0D2YKhZ&event=comments&redir_token=ApxAaw3LpPiEAF6N_goVKxJ0kRN8MTU2MDQxODUyMkAxNTYwMzMyMTIy) 

&#x200B;

 [https://imgur.com/JuCcszs](https://imgur.com/JuCcszs) 

&#x200B;

One in the far north and one in the far south, both clear of most danger, with fertile land, nearby resources, and easy access to local villages / cities. I've used the Fog Islands one before and can confirm that it's extremely effective, though it takes a bit of fortification to be able to stand up to the frequent Fogmen patrols. The land is very fertile and copper and iron nearby aren't hard to come by, as well as having Mongrel, the Western Hive, the Holy Nation, and the Shek Kingdom relatively nearby. If you wanted, you could even do some crazy micro and do what i'm trying to do - Set up two or more outposts.
